# jooby-codec invariants

- A command is an ESM module: `id`, `name`, `headerSize`, `examples`, `fromBytes(body)`, `toBytes(params)` (header+body). No command classes. File name is camelCase === `name`.
- `examples` on the command file are the hardware contract. Roundtrip tests must keep passing.
- Register commands **manually** in `message/{down,up}link.ts` (`toBytesMap` and `fromBytesMap`). Do not build maps via `Object.values` / iteration (Otto, QuickJS, TTN, Rollup).
- Bytes are `number[]` (`TBytes`). Use `BinaryBuffer`, not `Uint8Array` or `DataView`.
- MTX AES is `crypto-js` ECB NoPadding. Do not switch to `node:crypto` / WebCrypto.
- Analog headers are 1/2/3 bytes (`src/analog/utils/header.ts`). Do not “simplify”.
- MTX3 is an overlay of MTX1 (same wrappers). Shared MTX1 changes affect both.
- `plc` is compiled and `./*` can resolve `dist/plc`. It is not on `src/index.ts` and not in enumerated `package.json` exports. Do not add those unless asked.
- `DataSegmentsCollector` / `splitBytesToDataSegments` stay as deep imports (mtx-lora API), including the collector default export.
- `tsconfig` has `strict: false`. Do not enable `strict` in the same change as a feature.
- Deep imports (`jooby-codec/analog/commands/downlink/foo.js`) are public API.
- Keep existing `eslint-disable`. Do not introduce a Makefile or kebab-case command files.

```ts
// BAD — bundlers drop or keep the wrong commands
for (const cmd of Object.values(commands)) fromBytesMap[cmd.id] = cmd.fromBytes;

// GOOD
fromBytesMap[commands.softRestart.id] = commands.softRestart.fromBytes;
```
